Fix unhelpful GDMS auth error message (v0.118)

GDMS can return HTTP 200 with an error body (bad credentials, wrong
client_id/secret, wrong region, etc.) rather than a proper non-2xx
status. GdmsAuthService#send() only treated a non-2xx status as a
failure, so a 200-with-error-body response sailed through as a
"successful" call, and applyTokenResponse() then just found no
access_token and threw a bare "GDMS auth response did not contain an
access token" with no indication of what GDMS actually said - this is
exactly what showed up as the unhelpful "Live GDMS channel lookup
failed" message in Companies.tsx and in the container logs.

applyTokenResponse() now reuses describeAuthError() (previously only
used by send()'s non-2xx path) to pull GDMS's own msg/
error_description/error field out of the response body when
access_token is missing, and describeAuthError() itself now falls back
to including the raw response body (truncated to 500 chars) rather
than a bare "GDMS returned HTTP 200" when none of those fields are
present - so whatever GDMS is actually saying is visible in the UI and
logs without having to add debug logging and redeploy again.

